===Etymology 1===
Substantive noun from an [[ellipsis]] of the [[collocative]] term ''domus regia'' ("royal home/dwelling/abode"), itself from {{m|la|domus|t=house, home, abode, dwelling}} and {{m|la|rēgius|t=of or pertaining to a king; regal, royal}}. Compare origin of Greek {{l|grc|βασιλική||t=basilica}}, from {{cog|gkm|-}} term {{m|grc|[[βασιλική]] [[στοά]]||royal building}}.
.

